 Real-Time Kubernetes Issue & Resolution.

Issue: Pods remained in Pending state even though the cluster appeared healthy.

 ✔ Nodes were Ready
 ✔ No CPU or memory pressure
 ❌ Pods were not getting scheduled

🔍 Root Cause: A nodeSelector label mismatch between the pod specification and cluster nodes.

nodeSelector:
 env: production
But node labels were:

env=prod
This silent mismatch blocked pod scheduling.

 ✅ Solution:
 1️⃣ Verified node labels

kubectl get nodes --show-labels

2️⃣ Corrected the label mismatch

kubectl label node node-1 env=production

3️⃣ Pods scheduled successfully 🚀

🧠 Key Takeaway:

 Kubernetes doesn’t always surface clear errors for label mismatches.
 Even a small configuration difference can stop deployments entirely.

Always validate:

* nodeSelector
* node labels
* affinity rules

💡 Practical issues like these highlight why attention to detail matters in DevOps.
